<title>CANADA: Canada okays Eli Lilly schizophrenia drug.</title>
<headline>Canada okays Eli Lilly schizophrenia drug.</headline>
<dateline>TORONTO 1996-11-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pharmaceutical firm Eli Lilly Canada Inc, a unit of Eli Lilly and Co, said on Friday that the Canadian government approved its treatment for the mental illness of schizophrenia for use in Canada.</p>
<p>The drug Zyprexa, which can be used for the biologically based disease of the brain and other mental illnesses, has milder side effects than older medications, Eli Lilly said.</p>
<p>-- Lydia Zajc, Reuters Toronto Bureau (416) 941-8100</p>
